0	section	Talking to the Witch after creating the magnet
1	line	Witch	Hoorah for you, you have the magnet. Just hand it over to Ava. I'm working on my new recipe for spit-roast adventurer, so disturbing me isn't wise.
1	action	end
0	section	The bark has bite
0	section	Handing the magnet to Ava
1	line	Player	I've manufactured the magnet; here it is.
1	line	Ava	Great stuff! With the Witch's influence within the magnet, the undead chicken can use this, I'm sure.
1	line	Ava	The plan is that the chicken will operate the magnet to attract bits of iron and steel, maybe even your own recently fired arrows. There are plenty of totally lost arrowheads lying about in the fields of Gielinor, I bet.
1	line	Ava	In addition, arrows which you fire should be able to be attracted back to your quiver by the cunning avian.
1	line	Player	I begin to understand your plan. We've covered feathers and arrowheads now; what next?
1	line	Ava	We need a source of wood, but one which is spiritually active and can regenerate itself. That will save you some axework in the future.
1	line	Ava	Try using a woodcutting axe on the pesky trees in the garden here, the ones that attack rather than the really dead ones. They are probably just the sort of thing we could use.
1	line	Player	They will try to kill me, though, and I can't fight back!
1	line	Ava	Now you know how those poor guards feel when you hide behind mushrooms and fences and attack them from afar! Anyway, I reckon you'll need to try a mithril or better axe on the trees. At least the trees are
1	line	Ava	pretty close.
1	action	end
0	section	Talking to Ava before chopping at undead trees
1	line	Ava	So, what terrible hitch have you encountered now?
1	line	Player	Nothing really; I just decided to talk to you in case you have any great advice for me.
1	line	Ava	Well, I've heard that all kinds of dragons and even basilisks can drop mithril axes, if that's why you are delaying. Most of these creatures are silly enough that you can even hide behind something and plink them to
1	line	Ava	death in the brave ranger way.
1	action	end
0	section	Trying to chop an undead tree without mithril axe or better (or without carrying an axe)
0	section	Trying to chop an undead tree with mithril axe or better
0	section	Talking to the Witch after handing over the magnet
1	line	Witch	Hello my ickle...oh, it's you. What do you want?
1	line	Player	I wondered whether you had anything interesting to say.
1	line	Witch	Clearly not.
1	action	end
0	section	Returning to Ava
1	action	If While Guthix Sleeps has been completed, then Aya replaces Turael, with the same dialogue as Turael.
1	line	Player	Well, I tried to hack the trees with my axe, but it just bounced off the trunk! It did all seem all-too-convenient to work on the first try.
1	line	Ava	Fortunately for you, I've done some research and it seems to suggest that there are two choices open to you.
1	line	Player	Tell me the worst.
1	line	Ava	The first is more interesting. We cut off your arms, have them reanimated as undead, reattach them and then you should be able to cut the trees normally.
1	line	Ava	Of course, you won't be able to pick your nose any more, so I suppose you'll want to try the second option.
1	line	Player	I'm not exactly addicted to picking my nose, but I do think I'll pass on that method.
1	line	Ava	Well, in that case, I think it may have something to do with Slayer abilities. After all, I did see [Turael/Aya] poking around the trees while I was moving in.
1	line	Ava	As [he's/she's] not known for [his/her] random touristic activities, you should try chatting with this [Turael/Aya]. [He's/She's] the Slayer Master near Burthorpe.
1	line	Player	Oh dear, I hope [he/she] doesn't want me to buy one of [his/her] ridiculous fashion accessories. Those earmuffs [he/she] sells make heroic adventurers into a laughing stock.
1	action	end
0	section	A slayer's perspective
0	section	Turael
1	line	Turael	'Ello, and what are you after then?
1	option	I need another assignment.
1	option	Have you any rewards for me, or anything to trade?
1	option	Let's talk about the difficulty of my assignments.
1	option	I'm here about a quest.
2	line	Player	I'm here about a quest. Ava said she saw you hanging around the moving trees near Draynor Manor.
2	line	Turael	Ahh, you came to the right man; odd things, those trees. What is it you are needing exactly?
2	line	Player	I think I need some of the wood from them, but my axe just bounced off the trunk.
2	line	Turael	Sounds like you need a blessed axe. No one really makes them, though, these days.
2	line	Turael	Blessed axes are too soft to cut normal wood since the axe's edge must be replaced by holy silver. I can do you a favour, though.
2	line	Turael	If you can give me a mithril axe and a holy symbol of Saradomin I can let you have my axe. I'll make myself a new one when no one is pestering me for Slayer tasks.
2	line	Player	Okay, so I'll see whether I can spare an axe and a symbol. Thanks.
2	action	end
