0	section	Research and development
0	section	Delivering the twigs
1	line	Player	I have that undead wood at last. Well, twigs anyway.
1	line	Ava	You certainly took your time.
1	line	Player	I'd say they didn't grow on trees, but I guess you'd just be sarcastic about my sense of humour.
1	line	Ava	Quite. Now that we have all the ingredients for infinite arrows, we just need a container in which we can keep the components in the correct mutual alignment.
1	line	Ava	I've gathered together some research notes from various sources but I can't quite make out what they mean. If you want to have a go at making them out, just ask me for a copy.
1	action	end
0	section	Talking to Ava again
1	line	Player	I'd like to look at those research notes now, unless you have translated them without me?
1	line	Ava	They are still stumping me. Here are the notes; I really hope your head doesn't explode from reading them.
1	line	Player	I'd find it slightly inconvenient, I'm sure.
1	line	Ava	It wouldn't be all bad as your body would be useful for research after death. What I'd be upset about was if bits of you landed in my nice new bed.
1	line	Player	Your concern is touching.
1	action	end
0	section	Talking to Ava after losing the research notes
1	line	Player	I seem to have lost the research notes.
1	line	Ava	Don't tell me, your cat ate them? You won't get out of the job that easily; here are some copies I made.
1	action	end
0	section	Talking to Ava with the notes
1	line	Player	I have the notes but haven't translated them yet. Any hints?
1	line	Ava	I know you have the notes; I gave them to you, in case you forgot! Furthermore, if I had hints, I'd have translated those notes myself.
1	line	Ava	So, take the hint and go off and translate them. If it's too hard, you can always go and shoot demons in cages.
1	action	end
0	section	Reading the research notes
0	section	Successfully translating the notes
1	action	end
0	section	Talking to Ava after losing the translated notes
1	line	Ava	Let me guess, you've managed to mislay the notes after you translated them?
1	line	Player	I can't say I'm proud of it, but you aren't wrong.
1	line	Ava	Luckily, I assumed you were terminally careless, so I can supply these copies.
1	action	Ava hands over the untranslated research notes again.
0	section	The final component
0	section	Handing in the notes
1	line	Player	I've translated those notes. See? I'm not just a thuggish moron like you seem to think.
1	line	Ava	For all I know, it was pure luck, so don't jump to any conclusions about your mighty intellect.
1	line	Player	I can see why you don't have any assistants; you're not exactly easy to work with.
1	line	Ava	Let's get back to the work we're doing, then. Remember, this is all a favour to you; I could have just decided to fob you off with a feather duster.
1	line	Ava	I've given you a pattern for the container; you'll need to combine them with some polished buttons and hard leather. Then we're almost done. Good news, eh?
1	line	Ava	If you are having trouble finding buttons, I've heard rumours that the H.A.M. society carry this sort of stuff more than most.
1	line	Player	Really? How would you know this strange detail?
1	line	Ava	I hear they lose their clothes a lot to thieves so they have to make do with shoddy goods. Whatever the reason, they seem to carry buttons about in their pockets.
1	action	end
0	section	Talking to Ava again with the pattern
1	line	Player	So what do I do with this pattern again?
1	line	Ava	Your short-term memory loss worries me. Combine the pattern with hard leather and some polished buttons, then hand the resulting container to me.
1	action	end
0	section	Talking to Ava after losing the pattern
1	line	Player	The pattern seems to have vanished from my pack...not my fault, of course.
1	line	Ava	You're pretty careless, aren't you. I assume you're the type who leaves a trail of arrows and knives behind them when they train?
1	line	Ava	Here's a replacement; perhaps if I charged for them, you'd be more careful.
1	action	end
